# Local build output must never reach the Docker build context - Dockerfile copies each
# project's source directory wholesale (COPY src/<project>/ src/<project>/) *after* its own
# restore step already produced a fresh, RID-correct obj/project.assets.json inside the image.
# Without this, a local bin/obj left over from running `dotnet build`/`dotnet test` on the host
# (any OS/RID) gets copied on top of that fresh restore output, silently overwriting it -
# confirmed directly: this is exactly what caused a real local arm64 image build to fail with
# NETSDK1047 ("doesn't have a target for net10.0/linux-arm64") despite the container's own
# restore step succeeding and producing that exact target moments earlier.
**/bin/
**/obj/

.git/
.github/
